    "updated_at": "2026-02-11T14:29:38Z",
    "body": "> I vaguely recall promises not being a great building block for specifications, but I can't find the specific issue for this.\r\n\r\nIt's not super great for implementation sake either - it suddenly starts to depend on JS while the implementation otherwise wouldn't need to. Doing so implicitly makes things depend on JS Promise behavior.\r\n\r\nInterestingly the spec [creates a promise without defining what a promise is](https://fullscreen.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-element-requestfullscreen). (Filed https://github.com/whatwg/webidl/issues/1672)",
